From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seabraid <seabraid@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] seabraid: one channel per helper process, and a blob
 swap the helper writes and reads back

SEABRAID_STRATA_SHM is a comma-separated list, one channel per helper process; the
position is the card (remote_dev - kDeviceBase), fixed for the session.
seabraid::channel_name(card) is the one reader, used by preflight and
seabraid_open; an unset variable still means /seabraid0 for card 0.

RemoteExperts::seabraid_retier_blob sends the new expert's bytes through
channel blob slot 0 as one kTierSwapBlob op (wire v8), under read_mu_ so the
prompt path cannot reuse the slot, through the same fenced round as
seabraid_retier (now seabraid_round, which judges residency on the plain-swap
view of the ops). RemoteExperts::tier_verify reads a slot back with
ExpertCache::verify_slot and quarantines it on a mismatch; the helper calls it
after tier_sync and before the ack.

Failure: a refused op is untouched (kTierRejected), a torn or unread-back slot
is kTierFailed and closes the card, exactly as for a plain swap.
